        "original_id": "1e3d90b0-fc67-5095-97d5-be05141d6d07",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Carlton House, London\n- People: George IV, George III\n- Roles: Prince Regent, King of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland, King of Hanover\n\nFacts:\n- George IV was born as George Augustus Frederick on 12 August 1762.\n- Carlton House was a mansion in London and served as the town residence of the Prince Regent for several decades from 1783.\n- From 1811 until his accession, George IV served as Prince Regent during George III's final mental illness.\n- George IV became King of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland and of Hanover after George III died on 29 January 1820.\n- George IV died on 26 June 1830, ten years after his accession.",
